  "limitations": [
    "Pilot speed/altitude/assist conditions were not supplied; this demonstrates a native aircraft-law defect consistent with disturbance-driven hunting, not proof of the exact pilot scenario.",
    "24 s, 120 Hz development envelopes are regression limits, not validated F-35 handling specifications.",
    "Exactly neutral constant-gain starts remain quiet; zero pilot commands do not imply zero native feedback or zero physical disturbances.",
    "High-speed fixtures climb because they use one untrimmed development start across speeds; no level-flight trim or flight-envelope qualification is claimed.",
    "Partial-conversion and bank/deceleration diagnostic fixtures lose altitude with terrain forces excluded; they do not establish a safe transition or maneuver procedure.",
    "Manual bypasses the aircraft native stabilization law; host auto-trim and autopilot settings remain separate.",
    "Original aerodynamic coefficients, mass/CG/inertia assumptions and coupled LiftSystem approximation remain uncalibrated.",
    "No ground-contact, browser, sound device or supersonic qualification is part of this record."
  ]
